ns1:Persona-Autonomous_AI_Agent a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Autonomous_AI_Agent"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Autonomous_AI_Agent" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Autonomous_AI_Agent.md> ;
    skos:definition "The Autonomous AI Agent is an orchestration framework that coordinates specialized analytics and knowledge services to support decision-making. This very fast moving expertise is currently being used to create configurable workflows that integrate evidence from many data domains in both preclinical and clinical. Execution is scheduled and event-driven (e.g., on data updates or defined intervals) and can include sequential and parallel AI agents to deliver an agreed end goal such as literature retrieval, data summaries or analysis of data. It's success at the intended task depends on how the AI is instructed, the suitability of the AI model used and the FAIR characteristics of the underlying data—being findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable—with semantic standards (ontologies, identifiers), well-defined schemas and mappings, and machine-actionable metadata." ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Autonomous_AI_Agent.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText "The Autonomous AI Agent is an orchestration framework that coordinates specialized analytics and knowledge services to support decision-making. This very fast moving expertise is currently being used to create configurable workflows that integrate evidence from many data domains in both preclinical and clinical. Execution is scheduled and event-driven (e.g., on data updates or defined intervals) and can include sequential and parallel AI agents to deliver an agreed end goal such as literature retrieval, data summaries or analysis of data. It's success at the intended task depends on how the AI is instructed, the suitability of the AI model used and the FAIR characteristics of the underlying data—being findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable—with semantic standards (ontologies, identifiers), well-defined schemas and mappings, and machine-actionable metadata." .

ns1:Persona-Citizen_Data_Scientist a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Citizen_Data_Scientist"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Citizen_Data_Scientist" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Citizen_Data_Scientist.md> ;
    skos:definition "Non-expert business user applying self-service analytics tools and dashboards; highly competent but not data-science trained. Individual within an organization who, despite lacking formal training in data science, utilizes data analysis tools and techniques to extract insights from data. These individuals often come from various backgrounds, such as business, marketing, or operations, and possess domain-specific expertise. Citizen Data Scientists leverage self-service analytics platforms, intuitive data visualization tools, and automated machine learning algorithms and Autonomous AI agents to explore datasets, generate reports, and uncover patterns or trends relevant to their roles." ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Citizen_Data_Scientist.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText "Non-expert business user applying self-service analytics tools and dashboards; highly competent but not data-science trained. Individual within an organization who, despite lacking formal training in data science, utilizes data analysis tools and techniques to extract insights from data. These individuals often come from various backgrounds, such as business, marketing, or operations, and possess domain-specific expertise. Citizen Data Scientists leverage self-service analytics platforms, intuitive data visualization tools, and automated machine learning algorithms and Autonomous AI agents to explore datasets, generate reports, and uncover patterns or trends relevant to their roles." .

ns1:Persona-Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen.md> ;
    skos:definition "This role emerges  in organizations with high FAIR maturity (levels 4–5) and broad, well-curated data ecosystems, where interoperable, reusable data products are fully embedded into daily operations. Highly educated domain expert empowered by FAIR data products (e.g. query services, knowledge graphs) to find information in complex (FAIR) data sets daily decisions. Organization member who is empowered with access to information, possesses critical thinking skills, enabling them to contribute effectively to the organization’s goals and objectives." ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText "This role emerges  in organizations with high FAIR maturity (levels 4–5) and broad, well-curated data ecosystems, where interoperable, reusable data products are fully embedded into daily operations. Highly educated domain expert empowered by FAIR data products (e.g. query services, knowledge graphs) to find information in complex (FAIR) data sets daily decisions. Organization member who is empowered with access to information, possesses critical thinking skills, enabling them to contribute effectively to the organization’s goals and objectives." .

ns1:Persona-Legal_Data_Expert a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Legal_Data_Expert"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Legal_Data_Expert" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Legal_Data_Expert.md> ;
    skos:definition "Provides legal and regulatory expertise to ensure data is managed, shared, and reused in compliance with privacy, consent, and intellectual property requirements, while supporting FAIR-aligned practices across the organization.Has expertise in privacy law, data governance, and intellectual property; ability to draft and interpret data sharing agreements; experience in regulatory compliance and ethical data use in research and business contexts." ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Legal_Data_Expert.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText "Provides legal and regulatory expertise to ensure data is managed, shared, and reused in compliance with privacy, consent, and intellectual property requirements, while supporting FAIR-aligned practices across the organization.Has expertise in privacy law, data governance, and intellectual property; ability to draft and interpret data sharing agreements; experience in regulatory compliance and ethical data use in research and business contexts." .

