ns1:D3-L5 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Strategy at L5"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D3-L5" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level5.md#L103> ;
    rdfs:comment "FAIR is a widely understood organisational norm with a durable, transparent strategy. Measurable business outcomes, cost-benefit evidence, cross-functional integration and feedback guide investment, while relevant external stakeholders can see the strategy in practice."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L5 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """A company-wide vision and plan is supported and known and supported by all employees. FAIR is the norm, and everyone understands why FAIR data is needed. The company is also recognized for its FAIR data work and is a data-savvy company.

    FAIR data implementation strategy presents several crucial elements. There are clear links between FAIR data practices and tangible business outcomes, including cost savings, efficiency gains, and the identification of, e.g. business or IPR opportunities.

    Establishing Metrics and methodologies to measure these outcomes reinforces the strategy's connection to essential tools. Importantly, the organization comprehends the impact of FAIRness on its financial performance, prioritizing it as a part of its overarching business strategy, supported by empirical cost-benefit analyses.

    A high emphasis on Data integration facilitates the discovery of synergies by linking data across various business functions.

    The FAIR strategy is characterized by transparency, longevity, and effective measurement through metrics and feedback loops, aligning it with the organization's strategic imperatives.

    Outreach efforts to diverse stakeholders, including pharmaceutical companies, CROs, regulatory bodies, and academia, are also evident when relevant: strategy embodiments are externally visible.

    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**""" ;
    ns1:inDimension ns1:D3 ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level5.md#L103> .

ns1:D7-L0 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Tools and Infrastructures at L0"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D7-L0" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level0.md#L117> ;
    rdfs:comment "FAIR tooling, requirements and infrastructure roadmaps are lacking or poorly understood. Fragmented capture tools and ad hoc systems can impede FAIR implementation, with gaps in coordinated access and licensing arrangements."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L0 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """The organization presents a significant deficit in tools and infrastructure for implementing FAIR data management principles. Notably, the organization needs specialised tools, well-defined requirements, or a structured roadmap to ensure data adheres to the FAIR principles of Findability. Free field forms, e.g. in Excel documents, are frequent. This deficiency results in an unstructured and fragmented approach to data capture, undermining the organization's capacity to manage its data effectively. A pronounced lack of awareness and understanding of FAIR-compliant tools leads to a disjointed, ad-hoc problem-solving methodology that often contradicts FAIR principles. In the worst-case scenario, specific tools actively work against FAIR principles, exacerbating the challenge, especially when mandated by organizational processes, potentially coupled with geographical and web domain restrictions, further hindering the establishment of a robust FAIR data management framework. The organization must include an Inventory of the licences and access policy related to data sets.



    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**

    === "Findability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component which contributes, enhances or enriches Findability:
          
        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/findability-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/findability-maturity-indicators/)
            
        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/tool-data-granularity-and-context/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/tool-data-granularity-and-context/)

    === "Accessibility"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Accessibility.

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/accessibility-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/accessibility-maturity-indicators/)
      

    === "Interoperability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Interoperability.

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/interoperability-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/interoperability-maturity-indicators/)
    

    === "Reusability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Reusability.

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/reusability-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/reusability-maturity-indicators/)



![](images/new-pisto-logo-small.png)""" ;
    ns1:inDimension ns1:D7 ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level0.md#L117> .

ns1:Persona-Business_Owner a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Business_Owner"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Business_Owner" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Owner.md> ;
    skos:definition """The Business Owner is an executive-level business role accountable for the value, performance, and strategic success of a defined business process, product, system, or dataset. As the designated authority within their domain, the Business Owner ensures that data and processes deliver measurable business value, meet defined KPIs, and align with organizational objectives and regulatory requirements.

    In accordance with DAMA-DMBOK2, the Business Owner is responsible for defining business requirements, approving data standards and policies, and ensuring that data is managed as a strategic enterprise asset. They collaborate with Data Stewards, Architects, and IT teams to translate business needs into data capabilities, oversee the quality and fitness-for-purpose of data, and drive continuous improvement.

    By championing sound data governance and FAIR-aligned practices, the Business Owner ensures that information assets are consistent, compliant, and reusable—enabling efficient decision-making, regulatory confidence, and sustained business value generation across the organization.""" ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Owner.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText """The Business Owner is an executive-level business role accountable for the value, performance, and strategic success of a defined business process, product, system, or dataset. As the designated authority within their domain, the Business Owner ensures that data and processes deliver measurable business value, meet defined KPIs, and align with organizational objectives and regulatory requirements.

    In accordance with DAMA-DMBOK2, the Business Owner is responsible for defining business requirements, approving data standards and policies, and ensuring that data is managed as a strategic enterprise asset. They collaborate with Data Stewards, Architects, and IT teams to translate business needs into data capabilities, oversee the quality and fitness-for-purpose of data, and drive continuous improvement.

    By championing sound data governance and FAIR-aligned practices, the Business Owner ensures that information assets are consistent, compliant, and reusable—enabling efficient decision-making, regulatory confidence, and sustained business value generation across the organization.""" .

