ns1:D6-L2 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Knowledge at L2"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D6-L2" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level2.md#L164> ;
    rdfs:comment "Early roles, champions and prototype teams can explain and demonstrate FAIR value, but knowledge remains largely informal and held by individuals. Internal communities and external support begin to develop shared practices and organisation-specific training."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L2 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """Designated roles start to take shape in the company.

    FAIR knowledge is largely in people yet needs more formalization.

    The first champions and teams in prototypes can do it, explain it, prove value and start to get internal recognition.

    Community of practice also forms internally and facilitates knowledge exchanges ( for example, exchanges around emerging/good practices for FAIR and data Stewardship ).

    External resources help develop FAIR training based on the organization's specificities.

    Knowledge on processes, e.g. "FAIRification", what can be considered "FAIR" and what is not "FAIR"begins to be shared.

    "Vendors" (e.g. publishers) and "service providers" (e.g. CROs) curate, distribute, and generate data and play a role in the FAIR knowledge ecosystem.


    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**""" ;
    ns1:hasInterpretation ns1:interpretation-c396f8c5683c7cab6c5a873b ;
    ns1:inDimension ns1:D6 ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level2.md#L164> .

ns1:D6-L3 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Knowledge at L3"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D6-L3" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level3.md#L171> ;
    rdfs:comment "FAIR enters the training curriculum and business units begin formal knowledge sharing. Practitioners and communities build a common domain understanding and exchange implementation experience, at least within departments."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L3 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """FAIR data is part of the training curriculum, with some materials and experts available company-wide.

    Business Units begin the formalisation of FAIR knowledge sharing.

    Domain knowledge, providing a shared understanding and interpretation of data context within each domain, starts to be established.

    The Community of Practice drives domain knowledge through the common understanding and interpretation of data and its context.

    A community of knowledgeable FAIR practitioners have met and have started sharing experiences in making data FAIR, at least at the department level.


    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**""" ;
    ns1:hasInterpretation ns1:interpretation-5c1ca28f608f20a249f202d5 ;
    ns1:inDimension ns1:D6 ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level3.md#L171> .

ns1:Persona-FAIR_Community_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR_Community_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "FAIR_Community_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Community_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition """An individual or group responsible for facilitating and managing a community of practice (CoP). The organizer’s role involves coordinating meetings, events, and activities for the community, creating channels for communication and knowledge sharing, and fostering a supportive and inclusive environment where members feel comfortable exchanging ideas and experiences. They may also be involved in recruiting new members, setting goals and objectives for the community, and ensuring that it remains vibrant and relevant to its members’ needs and interests.

    Person who organizes groups of people around shared aims - see https://the-turing-way.netlify.app/collaboration/research-infrastructure-roles/community-manager.html\"""" ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Community_Manager.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText """An individual or group responsible for facilitating and managing a community of practice (CoP). The organizer’s role involves coordinating meetings, events, and activities for the community, creating channels for communication and knowledge sharing, and fostering a supportive and inclusive environment where members feel comfortable exchanging ideas and experiences. They may also be involved in recruiting new members, setting goals and objectives for the community, and ensuring that it remains vibrant and relevant to its members’ needs and interests.

    Person who organizes groups of people around shared aims - see https://the-turing-way.netlify.app/collaboration/research-infrastructure-roles/community-manager.html\"""" .

