ns1:D7-L1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Tools and Infrastructures at L1"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D7-L1" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level1.md#L149> ;
    rdfs:comment "Initial tooling plans and inventories identify FAIR gaps and requirements, while pragmatic templates and existing systems improve capture and curation. Early metadata centralisation, catalogues, identifier policies and reference-data or vocabulary tools begin to support findability."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L1 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """At this stage, there is an understanding of the data challenges and a recognition of the importance of FAIR data. Still, the organization needs to learn how to make it happen. Initial plans for tooling and infrastructure for POCs start to take shape, along with organizational buy-in.

    We see pragmatic progress in data and metadata creation and curation tools used to enhance existing IT practices (e.g. Excel templates, a drop-down list with limited selected items). There still needs to be complete FAIR tooling, but there is an inventory of the existing tooling and some determination of gaps along with the requirements for FAIR tooling.

    There is some centralization of metadata, e.g. with content management systems,ELN systems, e.g. DKAN. There may be a deployment of other systems such as Github, Drupal, Sharepoints.

    The organization starts thinking about and implementing "Findability" with Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) / Globally Unique, Persistent, Resolvable Identifier (GUPRI)services, published metadata catalogs, controlled vocabularies, Master Data Management (MDM) system (What needs to be "found"? Who needs to find what?). At least one policy on unique resource locators.

    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**

    === "Findability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component which contributes, enhances or enriches Findability:

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/use-cases/adoption-and-impact-of-an-identifier-policy-astrazeneca/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/use-cases/adoption-and-impact-of-an-identifier-policy-astrazeneca/)
          
        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/findability-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/findability-maturity-indicators/)
          

    === "Accessibility"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Accessibility.

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/accessibility-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/accessibility-maturity-indicators/)
      

    === "Interoperability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Interoperability.

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/interoperability-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/interoperability-maturity-indicators/)
    

    === "Reusability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Reusability.

        *   [https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/reusability-maturity-indicators/](https://fairtoolkit.pistoiaalliance.org/methods/reusability-maturity-indicators/)


![](images/new-pisto-logo-small.png)""" ;
    ns1:inDimension ns1:D7 ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level1.md#L149> .

