ns1:D7-L2 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Tools and Infrastructures at L2"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D7-L2" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level2.md#L183> ;
    rdfs:comment "In practical terms, D7-L2 describes early working FAIR infrastructure, potentially within individual departments. It covers tools for metadata publication, controlled vocabularies and persistent identifiers; configuring existing systems; working proofs of concept; and planning wider infrastructure, staffing and budgets."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L2 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """At this stage, the following are likely to be implemented (at least in some departments, do not need to be company-wide):Tools introduced to capture and publish metadata; Tools to work with controlled vocabularies; Tools to work with / manage persistent identifiers (PIDs).

    "FAIR data points" capturing and tooling may depend on the specific pharma function.

    Configure existing systems to implement FAIR, e.g., assigning PIDs to key documents, persons in organizational structures dealing with Human Resource, grant management, and publishing (authoring).

    The deployment of FAIR data maturity framework assessments (see "Lexicon")

    Initial infrastructure and tooling are in place for the first working POCs. Now that POCs work and prove value, RFPs or company-wide plans for tooling and infrastructure are getting scoped, including additional capacity for putting that infrastructure and tooling in place (people and budget).

    "Vendors", e.g. for ELN, play a key role in providing tools toward FAIR data principle implementation.

    The organization may look for reference "tools", e.g. controlled vocabularies, ontologies, data standards.


    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**

    === "Findability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component which contributes, enhances or enriches Findability:
          
        *   [Identifier Service](https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/Identifier-service)
        *   [Metadata schema](https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/Metadata-schema)
        *   [Registry](https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/Registry)

    === "Accessibility"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Accessibility.

        *   [Authorization&AuthenticationService](https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/Authentication-and-authorization-service)
      

    === "Interoperability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Interoperability.

        (less in focus at this stage)
    

    === "Reusability"

        Tool(s) or infrastructure component(s) which contributes, enhances or enriches Reusability.

        R is less in focus at this level, and usually not implemented.

![](images/new-pisto-logo-small.png)""" ;
    ns1:hasInterpretation ns1:interpretation-116912c078a12de1dbf03b3e,
        ns1:interpretation-17617bb80050545945e5b54b,
        ns1:interpretation-3fd7c849dc1329db0613751c,
        ns1:interpretation-4486f9bc68a7f960d9a87091,
        ns1:interpretation-5d25756965cbeac3a069a057,
        ns1:interpretation-5dd4a43fa117041e10b195f5,
        ns1:interpretation-70ff618aa8a786546a110095,
        ns1:interpretation-77710ddaf7e3c9a1645d6bc3,
