    ns1:evidenceStatus "requirement only; no operational test" .

ns1:D1-L3 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Descriptor ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Data at L3"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D1-L3" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level3.md#L66> ;
    rdfs:comment "FAIR data is working within departments or domains: local reference data, resolvable metadata, domain models and data-level access controls support integration, reuse and emerging self-service analytics. Broader organisational interoperability and reuse remain challenging."@en ;
    ns1:atLevel ns1:L3 ;
    ns1:evidenceStatus "not assessed" ;
    ns1:fullSourceBlock """One can find “FAIR” data in local environments such as a organization’s departments, divisions or functions.

    Data embeds local master and reference data. Metadata is identifiable and resolvable (at a local level), but data is still being determined (also at a local level).

    Data is “conformed” using a domain-level data model. It is integrated, processed and audited to support specific consumption patterns.

    While we achieve “Findability” and there is evidence of re-use at the local level, the "Interoperability" and "Reusability" principles are still a challenge in the broader scope of the organization.

    There are controls in place on Access at the data level.

    The creation of analytics-ready 'data-marts' enabling self-service analytics is under way.

    Machine interpretation is possible at the department level.

    Initial FAIR data sets are in production and proving value. There is a company-wide supported plan to make all (relevant) data FAIR. More data sets are bornFAIR while the company's budget and competencies grow. There is evidence of local reusability and, to some extent, interoperability.


    **[(Back to the FAIR Matrix)](FAIRMaturityMatrix.md)**""" ;
    ns1:hasInterpretation ns1:interpretation-1ada26269fbd4b9497f4ee3a,
        ns1:interpretation-334ec49879fa8ab7ea95e27e,
        ns1:interpretation-6195c4a79f369a411ca5de35,
        ns1:interpretation-6426e4701aefe33ffdb39d70,
        ns1:interpretation-7916e71608d980241cda8967,
        ns1:interpretation-8843479aa6da6c53cbcd82ca,
        ns1:interpretation-8c27840723aea8159a24d6d1,
        ns1:interpretation-99d8b7057d133902d19bcc41,
        ns1:interpretation-a0e274e6dbbb8c59214f5823,
        ns1:interpretation-a1ddae34a2c00794ee53f9d1,
        ns1:interpretation-b01dff4c56fb5f9586322961,
        ns1:interpretation-b48e43b061297d381b574cb1,
        ns1:interpretation-b9811d3738184ee01e0463a1 ;
    ns1:inDimension ns1:D1 ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/level3.md#L66> .

<https://w3id.org/fair/principles/terms/A1> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://w3id.org/fair/principles/terms/FAIR-SubPrinciple> ;
    rdfs:label "A1"@en ;
    dcterms:hasPart <https://w3id.org/fair/principles/terms/A1.1>,
        <https://w3id.org/fair/principles/terms/A1.2> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/fair/principles/latest/A1> ;
    skos:definition "(meta)data are retrievable by their identifier using a standardized communications protocol"@en .

ns1:D5 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:Dimension,
        ns1:Version125Dimension ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR Processes"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "D5" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/fmm-d5.md> ;
    skos:definition "FAIR data principles implementation requires underlying processes connecting the necessary metadata, data, tools, roles and knowledge. Some of these processes may be implicit in the early stages of FAIR data implementation. Still, they will become more explicit and so ubiquitous that they will become transparent once we achieve the highest maturity levels." ;
    ns1:inFrameworkVersion ns1:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    ns1:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/fmm-d5.md> ;
    ns1:sourceText "FAIR data principles implementation requires underlying processes connecting the necessary metadata, data, tools, roles and knowledge. Some of these processes may be implicit in the early stages of FAIR data implementation. Still, they will become more explicit and so ubiquitous that they will become transparent once we achieve the highest maturity levels." .

